---
// The Operate part of the Journey: what running a relay takes.
import LandingSection from './LandingSection.astro';

// "One container" stays out of this copy until someone follows the running-a-relay page on a clean machine
// (brand/91_EVIDENCE.md). The commands match that page, which pins the image tag in its compose file.
---

<LandingSection
  id="operate"
  heading="A relay on your own server."
  docs={{ href: '/docs/operate/running-a-relay', label: 'Run a relay' }}
>
  <p>
    The relay holds sealed bytes for devices that are offline, which in most families means Dad's phone. It drops them
    once they're delivered or expire. Back up its keypair once. Its SQLite file only holds messages waiting for
    delivery, so backing that up is optional.
  </p>

  <pre
    slot="aside"
    class="terminal"><span class="terminal__dim">$</span> docker compose up -d
<span class="terminal__dim">$</span> docker compose logs relay
<span class="terminal__dim"># the first start prints the relay's public key</span></pre>
</LandingSection>

<style>
  .terminal {
    margin: 0;
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--paper);
    white-space: pre-wrap;
    word-break: break-all;
    padding: 22px;
    font-size: 13px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  .terminal__dim {
    opacity: 0.6;
  }
</style>
